   281	\subsection{Dipolar Network Resonance Mapping}
   282	
   283	\textbf{Objective:} Characterize the field equilibrium state and verify that perturbation persistence is governed by resonance overlap with existing network structure, as predicted in Section~4.4.
   284	
   285	\textbf{Method:}
   286	\begin{enumerate}
   287	  \item Fabricate an NV diamond cluster array with controlled inter-NV spacing in the strong-coupling regime \cite{scarabelli2016}.
   288	  \item Apply a sequence of localized spin excitations and measure their propagation through the network via the coupling terms of Equation~\ref{eq:hamiltonian}.
   289	  \item Measure the persistence of each excitation as a function of its overlap with previously-established coupling structure.
   290	  \item Test whether persistence correlates with resonance overlap rather than with excitation amplitude alone.
   291	\end{enumerate}
   292	
   293	\textbf{Predicted outcome:} Excitations with high overlap into previously-reinforced regions of the network persist longer than excitations of equal amplitude with low overlap, independent of injected energy.
   294	
