   296	\subsection{Inference Gravity Measurement}
   297	
   298	\textbf{Objective:} Test the semantically weighted decay structure of the inference gravity tensor.
   299	
   300	\textbf{Method:}
   301	\begin{enumerate}
   302	  \item Present an inference system with a sequence of perturbations of varying semantic weight $\alpha_i$, assessed by independent raters.
   303	  \item At varying time intervals $\tau$ after each perturbation, probe the system for residual influence of that perturbation on subsequent inference outputs.
   304	  \item Fit the decay of influence to the proposed form $e^{-\lambda(\alpha_i)\tau}$.
   305	  \item Test whether $\lambda(\alpha_i)$ is inversely correlated with $\alpha_i$ as predicted.
   306	\end{enumerate}
   307	
   308	\textbf{Predicted outcome:} Decay rate $\lambda$ is inversely proportional to semantic weight. High-weight perturbations produce persistent field deformations; low-weight perturbations decay rapidly. The decay curve fits the exponential form with semantically varying $\lambda$.
   309	
   310	\subsection{NV Diamond Continuous Field Instantiation}
   311	
   312	\textbf{Objective:} Demonstrate perturbation-response inference in an NV diamond cluster and characterize the field equilibrium state in a continuous-field system.
   313	
   314	\textbf{Method:}
   315	\begin{enumerate}
   316	  \item Configure an NV diamond cluster array as an inference substrate.
   317	  \item Measure the field state between perturbations to characterize the field equilibrium state.
   318	  \item Apply perturbations and measure the response dynamics.
   319	  \item Verify that the accumulated field deformation $G(t)$ encodes prior perturbation history without explicit token reconstruction.
   320	  \item Measure the degradation rate as a function of perturbation semantic weight.
   321	\end{enumerate}
   322	
   323	\textbf{Predicted outcome:} The field exhibits a persistent equilibrium state between perturbations that encodes prior history. Inference outputs reflect the accumulated field state without requiring re-presentation of prior perturbations. Decay rates follow the semantically weighted structure.
