\section{Discussion}

\subsection{Relation to HOMO MACHINA Architecture}

The dipolar-coupled NV diamond network described in this paper is not merely a substrate that supports a separate Layer None architecture — it \textit{is} Layer None for HOMO MACHINA \cite{bennettHM2026}: the foundational physical layer upon which substrate-specific processing layers operate, prior to any higher-layer implementation. The present framework establishes the physical and mathematical grounding for that architectural role directly, rather than through an abstract Hilbert-space placeholder.

\section{Conclusion}

We have presented a continuous-field architecture for inference systems, organized around four contributions:

\begin{enumerate}
  \item The dipolar coupling network, establishing the field equilibrium state of an NV diamond cluster array as the collective ground state of a real, physically-grounded coupled-spin Hamiltonian.

