  \item Measure decay of any pre-existing field deformation $G(t)$ under this null condition across varying physical parameters: $^{13}$C isotopic concentration, paramagnetic impurity density, ambient temperature, and magnetic field stability.
  \item Fit observed decay to extract $\lambda_{\text{env}}$ in isolation, since the $k/\alpha_i$ term is structurally absent at $\alpha = 0$.
  \item Characterize the statistical properties of $\eta_{\text{env}}(t)$ — mean, variance, correlation time — across repeated trials and distinct physical samples.
\end{enumerate}

\textbf{Predicted outcome:} $\lambda_{\text{env}}$ is measurably nonzero and substrate-dependent, consistent with known $T_2$ dependence on isotopic purity \cite{balasubramanian2009}. This establishes an empirical floor below which Equation~\ref{eq:decay-generalized} cannot predict persistence, independent of semantic weight.

